  "title": "Sleep Is Not Optional",
  "emoji": "😴",
  "color": "#4C1D95",
  "description": "A tiny lesson with a big payoff: Sleep Is Not Optional.",
  "is_free": true,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "The world record for staying awake is 11 days. By day four, the person was hallucinating.",
      "visual": "👁️"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "Every animal with a nervous system sleeps—or enters a sleep-like state. Evolution demands it.",
      "visual": "🐾"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "During sleep, the brain clears toxic waste, consolidates memories, and repairs cellular damage.",
      "visual": "🧹"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "Rats deprived of sleep die within two to three weeks—faster than rats deprived of food.",
      "visual": "🐀"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "A rare genetic disease called fatal familial insomnia proves sleep is literally vital: patients die from sleeplessness.",
      "visual": "😱"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "Sleep isn't laziness. It's survival maintenance that your brain refuses to skip.",
      "visual": "🛡️"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "What happens to rats completely deprived of sleep?",
    "options": [
      "They die within two to three weeks",
      "They adapt and stop needing sleep",
      "They sleep with one eye open"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
